      "description": "Watch Norwich City vs Milton Keynes Dons highlights and goals from Carabao on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 8, 2026. On August 8, 2026, football fans gathered for a high-stakes Carabao Cup encounter that promised plenty of action from the opening whistle. The knockout nature of the competition set the stage for an intense battle between two sides eager to progress to the next round. A Fast Start for the Canaries Norwich City wasted no time establishing their dominance at home, striking within the first minute of play. Mohamed Touré found the top right corner with a clinical right-footed shot following a clever setup by Kenny McLean . The momentum stayed firmly with the hosts, and by the 7th minute, they doubled their lead. Anis Ben Slimane capitalized on another Touré involvement, slotting a right-footed effort into the bottom right corner to stun the visitors early on. The pressure from the home side remained relentless throughout the first half. Just before the break, in the 43rd minute, Ben Chrisene added a third goal for Norwich , firing high into the center of the net after being played in by Andre Brooks . The MK Dons struggled to find a foothold as the first period ended with the hosts firmly in command. Second Half Drama and Final Flourish The second half introduced a wave of drama when MK Dons were awarded a penalty in the 54th minute after Pelle Mattsson fouled Callum Paterson . However, Norwich goalkeeper Vladan Kovacevic produced a brilliant save to deny Nathaniel Méndez-Laing from the spot. The visitors did find a way back momentarily in the 56th minute, as Ryan Wintle converted from close range following a corner to make it 3-1. Any hopes of a comeback were swiftly extinguished just three minutes later. Andre Brooks got on the scoresheet himself in the 59th minute, finding the bottom corner to restore the three-goal cushion. Despite late efforts from MK Dons and several saves by Kovacevic in stoppage time, Norwich City maintained their composure to secure a convincing 4-1 victory and advance in the tournament."
